### How This Page Was Built

The image below shows the step **"This Website is One Guide"** being edited within **Visual Studio Code** using the **Docs Assembler** extension.

*   **Left (File Explorer):** The *DocumentationHell.tsmap* file is selected, showing the guide's structure.
*   **Center (Map View):** The step "**This website is One Guide**" is selected in the Map Editor.
*   **Right (Markdown Editor):** The content of the step is open for editing.

[<img class="nt-fr-big-image" src="/assets/images/ThisWebsiteIsOneGuide.png">](/assets/images/ThisWebsiteIsOneGuide.png)

#### The Power of Variables:

The step **"This Website is One Guide"** has an ancillary option **"Show this step..."**. Selecting it reveals the following view in Docs Assembler:

[<img class="nt-fr-mid-image" src="/assets/images/ShowThisStepAncillary.png">](/assets/images/ShowThisStepAncillary.png)

Notice line 8.  
It is a **variable**: 

[<img class="nt-fr-mid-image" src="/assets/images/ThisWebsiteIsOneGuideVariable.png">](/assets/images/ThisWebsiteIsOneGuideVariable.png)

On publish, a variable is automatically replaced with the variable's value. In this case it is markdown for an image link:

[<img class="nt-fr-big-image" src="/assets/images/ThisWebsiteIsOneGuideImageHtml.png">](/assets/images/ThisWebsiteIsOneGuideImageHtml.png)

